      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 4.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.4,
      "end_seconds": 10.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "no problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.04,
      "end_seconds": 28.99,
      "duration_seconds": 16.95,
      "text": "Erm, it's yellow eyes. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. I told my wife I'd come today. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.76,
      "end_seconds": 33.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.96,
      "end_seconds": 38.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "It's It's been ten days I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.07,
      "end_seconds": 41.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.99,
      "end_seconds": 48.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Dark urine goes along with it, most of the the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.36,
      "end_seconds": 51.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.7,
      "end_seconds": 59.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Anxiety for five years. Sorry I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.32,
      "end_seconds": 69.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "sure right so anxiety is already on your record we'll keep that in mind today what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.07,
      "end_seconds": 74.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.04,
      "end_seconds": 78.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.15,
      "end_seconds": 83.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.81,
      "end_seconds": 88.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.92,
      "end_seconds": 102.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "um I'm on escitalopram 10 milligrams once a day for the anxiety well though honestly some days I forget to take it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.86,
      "end_seconds": 116.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.44,
      "end_seconds": 121.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Hmm no not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.13,
      "end_seconds": 129.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any severe abdominal pain or bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.2,
      "end_seconds": 134.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "No none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.09,
      "end_seconds": 140.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "have you had any confusion fever or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.37,
      "end_seconds": 145.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "okay so no I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.12,
      "end_seconds": 151.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.43,
      "end_seconds": 156.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.34,
      "end_seconds": 169.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.9,
      "end_seconds": 185.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "that's it, just a little longer.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.26,
      "end_seconds": 212.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 121 over 68 respiratory rate 18 pulse is 83 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.48,
      "end_seconds": 217.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.72,
      "end_seconds": 222.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.08,
      "end_seconds": 239.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "the whites of your eyes are yellow and the liver edge is tender under the right ribs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.7,
      "end_seconds": 244.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.15,
      "end_seconds": 277.1,
      "duration_seconds": 25.95,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with an acute viral hepatitis at this stage. We should do a hepatitis screen for jaundice. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's book liver blood tests to look into jaundice. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.9,
      "end_seconds": 280.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.36,
      "end_seconds": 304.03,
      "duration_seconds": 21.67,
      "text": "No alcohol at all and avoid paracetamol and other painkillers unless we say. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. If you become drowsy or confused, that's the point to come in urgently. I'll want another look after the results. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.69,
      "end_seconds": 308.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}